I go to the next stall.
A man sells cheese here.
He has many different types of cheese.
He is currently cutting a large cheese.
The man sees me and smiles.
"Would you like to try?" he asks.
"Yes, gladly," I answer.
He gives me a small piece on a wooden stick.
I taste the cheese.
It is spicy and very delicious.
"I will take this," I say.
The seller wraps a large piece in paper.
"How much is that?" I ask.
"That is four euros and fifty cents," the man says.
I give him five euros.
He gives me fifty cents back.
"Thank you very much and have a nice weekend," he says.
I pack the cheese into my cloth bag.
